    regime: "The regime is still a physical energy supply shock priced through US real rates, but for the first time in this run two of its supporting legs wobbled on the same session. The dollar stopped beating everything - DXY 99.569 is down 0.07% and lost ground to five of seven peers - and bullion stopped falling, with gold up 0.87% and silver up 1.48% against a WTI that slipped 0.99%. Neither is yet a reversal: the dollar is still up 0.76% on the week against all seven, and gold is still down 1.56% on the week and 1.95% on the month. What it is, is a market flattening exposure before a dot plot. The second feature is that the calendar has collapsed into a single window - the Fed decides in twelve hours, New Zealand prints Q2 GDP five hours after that, the Bank of England votes in twenty-nine hours and the Bank of Japan in forty-four, and every one of them is priced: 86-90% on the Fed, 0.1% consensus on NZ GDP, 3-0-6 on the MPC, 97% on the BoJ. When every level is bought, the only tradeable content is guidance, and the only clean trades are the ones with no central bank attached to them.",
